mark wagner's volkswagen rolled off the  assembly line back in 1962.  it's definitely my daily driver and if  i'm going uh grocery shopping if i'm  going to hockey  if i'm  running errands like this is this is the  car while most beetles from the kennedy  era have long since made a one-way trip  to the junkyard wagner's runs like a  dream and fast too because this old  beetle is now an electric vehicle it's  clean it's quiet  it's reliable there's a lot less moving  parts and a lot less thing can go wrong  it's a joy to drive more and more owners  of broken down or mechanically  challenged classic cars are taking them  to shops like evie west  where owner mike bream and his expert  crew flipped them from fossil fuel to  electrons we remove the engine  in associated components so the fuel  tank the exhaust system  sometimes the transmission all of these  are replaced with an electric motor and  a tesla battery there seems to be no  shortage of tesla drivers wrecking their  cars and providing a plentiful supply of  parts  cars being retrofitted here include a  classic bmw a sleek black corvette and  even a gull wing delorean ready for a  trip back to the future the cost of an  electric overhaul ranges from eighteen  thousand to thirty thousand dollars  if you want to convert your classic car  to an electric vehicle you're gonna need  some patience  at this shop for example the waiting  list for new customers is five years  so our typical customer is one that  really loves their car either it has a  you know significance to the family  maybe it's been handed down or you know  a customer has driven it since high  school so typically  automotive enthusiasts best describes  our customers right now those customers  are also laughing at sky-high fuel  prices breem says he's concerned about  the environment and global warming but  reducing co2 emissions isn't his big  motivation i'm a motorhead i'm a hot  rodder i'm a speed guy wagner is proud  that his old vw isn't making the climate  crisis worse i'm excited to  take it up to the mountains driving  through the national forest not  polluting anything whether it's for  going green or going for speed classic  cars are getting a new electronic lease  on life  rob reynolds al jazeera san marcos  california
 

